hello everybody it's that time of year  again we're close to the end of 2021 and  so it's time to solicit suggestions and  then we'll do a vote  for some of the authors for the worlds  of speculative fiction series coming up  in 2022 now some people might be a  little confused what's the worlds of  speculative fiction it's a series that i  originally did in person and then video  recording and then eventually in covid  time shifted to all online that began in  2016  and is continuing on to the present  we've covered a lot of authors a lot of  texts and the focus is on exploring  philosophical themes and narrative  worlds so you know looking for example  at the lord of the rings and middle  earth or the alliance union universe of  cj chera or all sorts of other things  where there's a shared narrative  universe that we can explore  so i have some  authors and texts already lined up  mostly series in fact  going all the way from january to  september so nine different  installations for 2022 but i want some  some suggestions some input from you  the people who might be interested in  what other sessions we could do for the  other three sessions of 2022  now i'm going to tell you who we're  covering in 2022 in just a moment i do  want to remind you before you make your  suggestions you want to go to the worlds  of speculative fiction playlist and see  whether the thing that you're tempted to  suggest has already been  covered if it has then there will be a  video or sometimes videos about it for  instance if you're going to suggest our  scott backers prince of nothing series  we covered that this year with three  different installations or ursula k le  guin's earth c series that i think we  did last year with two different  installations so you want to make sure  that the suggestions that you're giving  are things we  haven't already explored and then what  i'm going to do  is take the suggestions that you leave  in your comments  and i'll go through and see whether  there's any that are getting a lot of  traction and i'll come up with a list of  the top six  and then you get to vote on  those maybe maybe i'll actually do top  four we'll see it depends on how i set  up the survey but you get input at two  different points first giving  suggestions  and then we winnow those and come up  with the best suggestions for a vote and  the top votes will get into  the series for next year so series for  next year who are we covering  i have been a little bit stalled in  reading through a  fan suggestion book that is very long  and very dense neil stephenson's anathem  and i'm gonna do that one in january i  had intended originally to do it in  november and then i kicked it down to  december of this year but we're gonna do  it in january and start out with that  then in february we're going to do  phillip pullman's his dark materials  trilogy northern lights the subtle knife  the amber spy glass so if you're into  that that is a session you won't want to  miss  march we're going to do octavia's but  octavia butler's parable novel so we're  coming back to butler who we've already  done with our xenogenesis series parable  of the sower parable of the talents  in april we'll we'll be taking on a  fan suggested one that people have been  asking for for quite a while olaf  stapleton also a philosopher so i'm  really looking forward to delving into  his works we're going to do three of his  novels last and first men last men in  london and star maker and then in may  we're going to do veronica roth's carve  the mark series which includes carve the  mark the fates divide and then some of  the stories in the end and other  beginnings i actually got to meet roth a  couple years ago when she was on a book  tour for the end and other beginnings  and i  co-presented with her here in milwaukee  at boswell books a really fun  time you know i enjoyed these stories so  we're going to go into those then in  june we're going to go way back into the  archives and continue something that we  started in the very first year  so roger zelazny  did  the chronicles of amber and we talked  about the first five books that center  around  one main character and a bunch of other  characters of course  introducing ideas of law and chaos and  all sorts of cool things like that  we're going to continue that one in june  with the  the five following stories that center  instead of around corwin they center  around merlin his son trumps of doom  blood of amber sign of chaos night of  shadows prince of chaos those were  coming out while i was in high school  and college i really enjoyed them so  hopefully you know they hold up over  time in july we're going to return to  something that i've been promising to do  for a long time people have been asking  about jg ballard so we're going to look  at his modern dystopias with crash  concrete island and high rise in august  we're going to come back to philip k  dick somebody who we've done several  times this time we're going to be  focusing on the theme of androids and  humans and looking at his speech  of the the same name so we're going to  look at we can build you to android's  dream of electric sheep the simulacrum  and some of the short stories like  imposter and nanny and we'll probably  add some to the list in september  margaret atwood's gilead dystopia  stories the handmaid's tale and her  recently published the testaments and  that takes us up to the fourth quarter  of the year where you get to have some  input into what we'll be  doing you can help decide what other  text authors narrative universes we  ought to go into so leave your comments  below again make sure that you  look at the worlds of speculative  fiction playlist so that you're not  suggesting something that we've already  covered  try to suggest something new something  that you're interested in something that  you'd like me to tackle and to go into  the philosophical themes and narrative  universe and discuss and like and then  offer as i do i create a video and then  i offer a session after the video for us  to engage in video conferencing  discussion about it so that's it  the job for you is to  take a look at what's already been done  see what you would like to have added  for the last three sessions of the  worlds of speculative fiction coming up  in 2022 and tune in if any of these  sounded interesting to you right we're  doing uh neil stephenson phillip pullman  octavia butler ola stapleton veronica  roth roger zelazny jg ballard phillip  dick and margaret atwood next year if  any of those sound interesting to you  then put it on your calendar you can  find  when and where these are going to be on  the reason io calendar right available  at reasonio.com  you can find them on my facebook page  once i actually put them up there i  announce these well in advance so you  know they're always on on saturdays  usually beginning at noon central time  so you have a lot of opportunity to  participate in these i hope that you've  got some interesting suggestions for me  and i look forward to seeing what you  have to say  you
 

